sentences.t:
Mas yo vos diré d' aquel Félez Muñoz;
sobrino era del Çid Campeador;
mandáronle ir adelante mas de s[o] grado non f[o].

sentences.l:
But I to-you will-tell of that Félez Muñoz;
nephew he-was of-the Çid Campeador;
they-ordered-him to-go ahead but of his will not it-was.

On the road where he-was-going pained-him the heart,
from all the others apart himself he-went-out,
into a wood thick Félez Muñoz himself put,

sentences.t:
Víolos venir e o[d]ió una razón,
ellos nol vi[di]en ni dend sabien ración;
sabed bien que si ellos le vi[d]iessen, non escapara de mu[o]rt.

sentences.l:
He-saw-them come and heard a speech,
they not-him were-seeing nor of-it were-knowing portion;
know-ye well that if they him had-seen, not he-would-have-escaped from death.

sentences.t:
Valas tornando a ellas amas a dos;
tanto son de traspuestas que nada dezir non pu[o]den.
Partiéronsele las telas de dentro del coraçón,

sentences.l:
He-goes-them turning to them both two;
so-much they-are of senseless that nothing to-say not they-can.
Parted-themselves-to-him the membranes from within of-the heart,

sentences.t:
A Sant Estevan vino Félez Muñoz,
falló a Dí[a]g Téllez el que de Albar Fáñez f[o];
quando elle lo o[d]ió, pesól de coraçón;

sentences.l:
To Sant Estevan came Félez Muñoz,
he-found Dí[a]g Téllez, he who of Albar Fáñez was;
when he it heard, it-grieved-him from heart;

sentences.t:
Alabándos se[d]ían ifantes de Carrión.
Por todas essas tierras estas nuevas sabidas son;
de cuer peso esto al buen rey don Alfons.

sentences.l:
Praising-themselves were Infantes of Carrión.
Through all those lands these tidings known are;
from heart grieved this to-the good king don Alfons.

sentences.t:
Van aquestos mandados a Valençia la mayor;
quando gelo dizen a mio Çid el Campeador,
una grand ora penssó e comidió;
alçó la su mano, a la barba se tomó;

sentences.l:
Go these tidings to Valençia the great;
when it-to-him they-tell to my Çid the Campeador,
one great hour he-thought and pondered;
he-raised the his hand, to the beard himself he-took;

sentences.t:
par aquesta barba que nadi non messó,
non la lograrán ifantes de Carrión;
que a mis fijas bien las casaré yo!”

sentences.l:
by this beard which nobody not plucked,
not it shall-enjoy Infantes of Carrión;
for my daughters well them shall-marry I!”

sentences.t:
Cavalgó Minaya con Per Vermu[doz]
e Martín Antolínez, el Burgalés de pro,
con dozientos cavalleros, quales mio Çid mandó;

sentences.l:
Rode Minaya with Per Vermu[doz]
and Martín Antolínez, the Burgalese of worth,
with two-hundred knights, such-as my Çid ordered;

sentences.t:
mucho vos lo gradeçe, allá do está, mio Çid el Canpeador;
assí lo ffago yo que aquí estó.
Affé Dios de los çielos que vos de dent buen galardón!”

sentences.l:
much to-you it thanks, there where he-is, my Çid the Campeador;
so it do I who here am.
Behold God of the heavens, that to-you may-give for-it good reward!”
